# Plan (and, unless dry_run, execute) a grasp of the target at a TF frame: open the gripper, move above it, descend
# straight down onto it, close the gripper, lift. The WHOLE sequence is planned first: if any leg is unreachable or
# the Cartesian legs deviate too much, nothing moves. Heights and gripper values: config/grasp.yaml (flagged defaults).
string target_frame      # TF frame of the target in base_link; its +z is the surface normal (up for a floor marker)
bool dry_run             # plan and check only: the arm and the gripper do not move
---
bool success             # dry run: the plan is feasible; otherwise: the sequence was accepted and started (see ~status)
string message
float64 plan_duration_s  # predicted time of all the motions
float64 max_cartesian_deviation_m
